Tests pass. Change made in `src/weights.ts:10-15`:

```ts
export function memoryBudget(bytes: number, overhead: number = 0.1, category?: string) {
  const allocated = entryWeight(bytes, overhead, category);
  const available = Math.max(0, 1048576 - allocated / byteUnit);
  const overBudget = allocated / byteUnit > 1048576;
  return { allocated, available, overBudget };
}
```

`allocated` and `available` are preserved; `overBudget` is added as a boolean flag that is `true` only when the allocated bytes exceed the 1048576 cap (where `available` is clamped to 0). Existing callers in `src/lru.ts:63` (`cacheHeadroom`) and `src/weights.ts:16` (`remainingBudget`) are unaffected.

